{
  "id": "environment",
  "title": "Marking development mode",
  "group": "Tooling",
  "summary": "The development server marks every document that it serves as development. A view reads that mark as `page.development`. Here the view passes it to a service method, so the service decides which content a published bundle should not show. This works in every service language: a service in a language other than JavaScript or TypeScript has no DOM, but its methods take arguments from the view. A JavaScript or TypeScript service can also read the mark itself from `document.body.dataset.tachyonEnvironment`. A published bundle can never say that it is in development, wherever it is hosted.",
